  "content": "[Intro]\n[A]\nI saw her today,\n\n[Verse 1]\n[A]I saw her\nface, it was a face I\n[F#m]loved, and I knew\nI had to run\n[A]away, and\nget down on my knees and pray\n[F#m]that they'd go\naway But still they'd begin,\n\n[Chorus]\n[A]\nneedles and pins\n[F#m]\nBecause of all my\n[D]pride,\nthe tears I gotta\n[E]hide\nHey I thought I was smart,\n\n[Verse 2]\n[A]I'd won her\nheart Didn't think I'd\n[F#m]do , but now I\nsee She's worse to him than\n[A]me, let her go\nahead Take his love in-\n[F#m]stead, and one day she will\nsee Just how to say plea-\n\n[Chorus]\n[A]se,\nand get down on her\n[F#m]knees\nHey that's how it begins,\n[D]\nshe'll feel those needles and pins\n[E]Ahurtin' her,\nahurtin' her [E][D#][D]\n\n[Bridge]\n[C#]Why can't I stop\nand tell myself I'm\n[B]wrong, I'm wrong, so\nwrong\n[A]Why can't I stand\nup and tell myself I'm\n[G#]strong\nBecause I saw her today,\n\n[Verse 3]\n[Db]I saw her\nface, it was a face I lo-\n[Bbm]ved, and I knew\nI had to run\n[Db]away, and\nget down on my knees and pray\n[Bbm]that they'd go\naway But still they'd begin\n\n[Chorus]\n[Db]\nneedles and pins\n[Bbm]\nBecause of all my\n[Gb]pride,\nthe tears I gotta\n[Ab]hide\nOh needles and pins\n\n[Outro]\n[Db],\nneedles and pins\n,\nneedles and pins",
